# Guard rail: `railway up` uploads from the repo root (the linked project path),
# so the Foundry artifacts and the .env holding PRIVATE_KEY would otherwise be
# swept in. Each service then builds from its own Root Directory setting
# (covenant-web -> /frontend, covenant-api -> offchain/).
#
# The directory entries below are anchored with a leading slash on purpose.
# These follow gitignore semantics, where an unanchored `lib/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth -- which silently stripped
# frontend/src/lib/ out of the upload and broke the web build with
# "Cannot find module '../lib/format'". Anchored, they match only the repo root.
/out/
/cache/
/broadcast/
/.scratchpad/
/lib/
/test/
/video/

# Deliberately left unanchored: these should never ship from anywhere in the tree.
.env
.env.*
node_modules/
*.pdf
